<title>USA: NEC cuts commercial desktop systems prices.</title>
<headline>NEC cuts commercial desktop systems prices.</headline>
<dateline>MOUNTAIN VIEW, Calif. 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>NEC Computer Systems, a subsidiary of NEC Corp, said it would cut prices of its high-performance desktop systems by up to 18 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;This price reduction demonstrates our commitment to deliver industry-leading solutions at very competitive prices,&quot; Murali Dharan, NEC vice president of Desktop Systems, said in a statement.</p>
</text>
